mastery.solution_text:
The horizontal dilation does not change the range, and the translation adds $\frac{\pi}{4}$ to each asymptote.
$y=\frac{\pi}{2}+\frac{\pi}{4}=\frac{3\pi}{4}$
$y=-\frac{\pi}{2}+\frac{\pi}{4}=-\frac{\pi}{4}$
For the $y$-intercept, substitute $x=0$.
$y=\arctan 0+\frac{\pi}{4}=\frac{\pi}{4}$
For the $x$-intercept, set $y=0$.
$\arctan(2x)=-\frac{\pi}{4}$
$2x=-1$
$x=-\frac{1}{2}$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=1.35cm, y=1.3cm]
\draw[->] (-2.4,0) -- (2.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1.3) -- (0,2.9) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[dashed] (-2.3,2.3562) -- (2.3,2.3562);
\draw[dashed] (-2.3,-0.7854) -- (2.3,-0.7854);
\draw[thick,<->,domain=-2.3:2.3,samples=100,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{rad(atan(2*\x))+0.7854});
\fill (0,0.7854) circle (2pt);
\fill (-0.5,0) circle (2pt);
\draw (-0.5,0.07) -- (-0.5,-0.07);
\node[below,font=\small] at (-0.5,-0.07) {$-\frac{1}{2}$};
\draw (0.06,0.7854) -- (-0.06,0.7854);
\node[left,font=\small] at (-0.09,0.7854) {$\frac{\pi}{4}$};
\node[font=\small,above] at (-1.5,2.3562) {$y=\frac{3\pi}{4}$};
\node[font=\small,below] at (-1.5,-0.7854) {$y=-\frac{\pi}{4}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
